# Numerical evaluation of the chamber density

The chambers of lift `L` are the forward chambers `fcells` (walls `walls1`, `walls5`); for `L < 20`
some chambers carry the (better) dual bound, recorded in `dualTab` as `some (m, j)` with `j` the
index of the certifying `DCell` in `dcells0 ++ ⋯ ++ dcells11` (generated by work/gen_density.py).

The density `½ Σ_{L < L2} Σ m (1/(L+lo) - 1/(L+hi))` is evaluated exactly (rounded down termwise)
for `L < 100` and bounded by telescoping for `100 ≤ L < L2`.
